IMPORT prelude

-- Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 (NT) -- the Territory's no-fault scheme for death or injury in a motor accident,
-- with the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Regulations 1984 (NT) that set its alcohol presumption, impairment guides,
-- attendant care criteria and commutation.
--
-- SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE. The rules are written in the Act's own actors and terms: "the injured person", "the eligible person",
-- "the qualifying person", "the claimant", "the Commission", "the designated person". The questions of the person injured are in
-- maca-seat.l4; the questions of those left after a death (the spouse, the dependent children, the dependent parents and the
-- person liable for the funeral) are in maca-seat-survivors.l4. Both IMPORT this module and restate no rule.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. Act: s 4 (motor vehicle, Territory motor vehicle, spouse, dependent child, dependent parent, average
-- weekly earnings, as inputs where the Act borrows a figure), s 4A, s 4B, s 4C (as the Commission's assessment), s 4DA (as
-- facts), s 7, s 9, ss 9A-9G, s 10, ss 10A-10C, s 11, s 11A, s 11B, s 13(1), (2), (2A), (3) (see the formula note), (5), (5A),
-- s 14, s 17, s 18 (whether a service is covered), ss 18BA-18BE (eligibility only), s 20, s 20A, s 21, s 22, s 23, s 24,
-- s 25, s 28A, s 28B, s 28E, s 31, s 31A, s 37, s 46, s 47, s 49. Regulations: reg 3 ("(indexed)"), reg 4 (AMA Guides, 6th
-- edition, as a fact), reg 4A, reg 4B (as a fact), reg 4D (as the Commission's judgment), regs 4E, 4F (eligibility), reg 4M,
-- reg 5, reg 6.
--
-- THE LOST FORMULA. s 13(3) reads "the Commission must calculate the amount ... in accordance with the following formula:"
-- and then "where: X is ... and MA is ...". The formula itself did not survive conversion of the Word reprint. The weekly
-- amount the Commission calculates under s 13(3) is therefore an INPUT, bounded by MA; the nil cases of s 13(2)(b) and (5) are
-- encoded. See NOTES.md, finding 1.
--
-- FIGURES NOT IN ANY DEPOSIT, taken as INPUTS: average weekly earnings (s 4: the ABS full-time adult ordinary time earnings for
-- the Territory, last published before 1 January of the calendar year); the s 13(2)(a) maximum amount MA, determined by the
-- Commission for each half-year; the CPI figures for the reg 3 "(indexed)" amounts; the day a person reaches pension age
-- (Social Security Act 1991 (Cth) s 23); what the Traffic Regulations 1999 reg 19(2) require of a driver.
--
-- EDITION. Act: reprint REPM022, as in force at 31 May 2019, deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/Motor-Accidents-Compensation-Act-1979-NT-current-reprint-REPM022.txt. It is the oldest reprint
-- in the NT sample and older than the Regulations, so an amendment to the Act after 31 May 2019 may be missing. Regulations:
-- reprint REPM022R1, as in force at 28 August 2026, deposited at ../../../motor-accidents-compensation-regulations-1984/
-- registers/source-bundle/Motor-Accidents-Compensation-Regulations-1984-NT-current-reprint-REPM022R1.txt.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL COPY. The statutory words quoted in comments are not an official version of the Act or the Regulations.
-- Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is owned by the Northern Territory; reproduced under the NT copyright policy of
-- 8 October 1996 (not an official version, no use of the NT arms, accurate reproduction in a context that does not mislead),
-- and quoted in this encoding under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (see SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
--
-- BASELINE. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, design defaults of 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 (NT) -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `Days and dates`

-- Dates are compared by their serial day numbers.
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE
      `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is before` `the second day` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE
      `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is on or after` `the second day` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the first day` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `n` IS A NUMBER
      `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `n` `days after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE
      `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE
      `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` `the first day` `and` `the second day` MEANS
    IF `the first day` `is before` `the second day`
    THEN `the second day`
    ELSE `the first day`

-- A sortable number for a calendar day: year, month, day.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the calendar key of` `the day` MEANS
    (DATE_YEAR `the day` TIMES 10000) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the day` TIMES 100) PLUS DATE_DAY `the day`

-- Completed years of age. READING: a person born on 29 February has a birthday on 1 March in a common year.
GIVEN `the birthday` IS A DATE
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the age of a person born` `the birthday` `on` `the day` MEANS
    IF ((DATE_MONTH `the day` TIMES 100) PLUS DATE_DAY `the day`) LESS THAN ((DATE_MONTH `the birthday` TIMES 100) PLUS DATE_DAY `the birthday`)
    THEN (DATE_YEAR `the day` MINUS DATE_YEAR `the birthday`) MINUS 1
    ELSE DATE_YEAR `the day` MINUS DATE_YEAR `the birthday`

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` `the year` IF
        ((`the year` MODULO 4) EQUALS 0 AND (NOT ((`the year` MODULO 100) EQUALS 0)))
    OR  (`the year` MODULO 400) EQUALS 0

GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the year`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in month` `the month` `of` `the year` MEANS
    IF `the month` EQUALS 2
    THEN IF `is a leap year` `the year` THEN 29 ELSE 28
    ELSE IF `the month` EQUALS 4 OR `the month` EQUALS 6 OR `the month` EQUALS 9 OR `the month` EQUALS 11
         THEN 30
         ELSE 31

-- The same day a number of months later. READING: where that month is shorter, its last day (31 August plus 6 months is
-- 28 or 29 February; 29 February plus 3 years is 28 February). The Act does not say.
GIVEN `months`    IS A NUMBER
      `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `months` `months after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY `the start`) (`the number of days in month` `the month` `of` `the year`)) `the month` `the year`
    WHERE
        `the month index` MEANS ((DATE_MONTH `the start`) MINUS 1) PLUS `months`
        `the month` MEANS (`the month index` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        `the year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS FLOOR (`the month index` DIVIDED BY 12)

-- Saturday or Sunday. DATE_SERIAL of Friday 31 May 2019 is 737574, which is 5 modulo 7; so Saturday is 6 and Sunday 0.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `falls on a weekend` `the day` IF
        (DATE_SERIAL `the day` MODULO 7) EQUALS 6
    OR  (DATE_SERIAL `the day` MODULO 7) EQUALS 0

-- The n-th weekday (Monday to Friday) after a day.
GIVEN `n`       IS A NUMBER
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the weekday` `n` `weekdays after` `the day` MEANS
    IF `n` AT MOST 0
    THEN `the day`
    ELSE IF `falls on a weekend` `the next day`
         THEN `the weekday` `n` `weekdays after` `the next day`
         ELSE `the weekday` (`n` MINUS 1) `weekdays after` `the next day`
    WHERE
        `the next day` MEANS `the day` 1 `days after` `the day`

§§ `Amendment dates that limit this encoding (ss 46, 47, 49)`

-- s 46(1): "Part 3, as amended by the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Amendment Act 2014, applies only in relation to motor
-- accidents that occurred after commencement"; (2): the earlier Part 3 "continues to apply" to earlier accidents. s 47: the same
-- for ss 18 and 19. That Act "Commenced | 1 July 2014" (endnotes). s 18BA: Subdivision 2 "applies in relation to an injury
-- suffered on or after 1 July 2014". The earlier text is not deposited.
`the 2014 amendments commenced` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2014

-- s 49(1): "Section 13, as amended by the Motor Accidents (Compensation) Amendment Act 2019, applies only in relation to a motor
-- accident that happens after the commencement"; (2): the earlier s 13 "continues to apply" to earlier accidents. That Act
-- "Commenced | 31 May 2019". READING: an Act commences at the start of the day, so an accident on 31 May 2019 happens after the
-- commencement. The earlier s 13 is not deposited.
`the 2019 amendments commenced` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 31 5 2019

§§ `s 4 -- motor vehicle and Territory motor vehicle`

-- s 4: "motor vehicle means a vehicle designed to be self-propelled and includes a trailer when attached to such a vehicle but
-- does not include: (a) a vehicle that runs on rails; or (b) a motorised wheelchair that is not capable of travelling at a speed
-- greater than 10 km/h; or (c) a cycle powered by an engine with a power output not exceeding 200 watts."
DECLARE `Vehicle` HAS
    `is designed to be self-propelled, or is a trailer attached to such a vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
    `runs on rails`                                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a motorised wheelchair not capable of more than 10 km/h`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a cycle powered by an engine of no more than 200 watts`                    IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the vehicle` IS A `Vehicle`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a motor vehicle` `the vehicle` IF
        `the vehicle`'s `is designed to be self-propelled, or is a trailer attached to such a vehicle`
    AND (NOT `the vehicle`'s `runs on rails`)
    AND (NOT `the vehicle`'s `is a motorised wheelchair not capable of more than 10 km/h`)
    AND (NOT `the vehicle`'s `is a cycle powered by an engine of no more than 200 watts`)

-- s 4: "Territory motor vehicle means a motor vehicle currently registered under the Motor Vehicles Act 1949 and includes a motor
-- vehicle currently registered under the Interstate Road Transport Act 1985 (Cth) where the vehicle was last registered (or
-- re-registered) in the Territory." Registration under those Acts is a borrowed term, asked as a fact.

§§ `s 4A -- motor accidents`

-- s 4A(1): "A motor accident is an occurrence: (a) caused by or arising out of the use of a motor vehicle; and (b) resulting in
-- the death of, or injury to, a person." (2): it is caused by or arises out of the use of a motor vehicle "if, and only if, it
-- results directly from: (a) the driving of the motor vehicle; or (b) the motor vehicle moving out of control; or (c) a
-- collision, or action to avoid a collision, with the motor vehicle (whether the motor vehicle is stationary or moving)."
-- (3): a person who "renders assistance, or attempts to render assistance, at the scene of a motor accident" and as a result
-- dies or is injured: "the accident is taken to have resulted in the death or injury".
DECLARE `Occurrence` HAS
    `the vehicle`                                                                          IS A `Vehicle`
    `resulted directly from the driving of the vehicle`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `resulted directly from the vehicle moving out of control`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `resulted directly from a collision, or action to avoid a collision, with the vehicle`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was killed or injured in it`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was killed or injured rendering assistance at the scene`                    IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the occurrence` IS AN `Occurrence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is caused by or arises out of the use of a motor vehicle` `the occurrence` IF
        `is a motor vehicle` (`the occurrence`'s `the vehicle`)
    AND (    `the occurrence`'s `resulted directly from the driving of the vehicle`
         OR  `the occurrence`'s `resulted directly from the vehicle moving out of control`
         OR  `the occurrence`'s `resulted directly from a collision, or action to avoid a collision, with the vehicle`)

GIVEN `the occurrence` IS AN `Occurrence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the death or injury results from a motor accident` `the occurrence` IF
        `is caused by or arises out of the use of a motor vehicle` `the occurrence`
    AND (    `the occurrence`'s `the person was killed or injured in it`
         OR  `the occurrence`'s `the person was killed or injured rendering assistance at the scene`)

§§ `s 4B -- residents of the Territory`

-- s 4B(1): a person is, at the time of a motor accident, a resident of the Territory "if the person has resided in the Territory
-- for a continuous period of at least 3 months". (2): "However, a person is not to be regarded as a resident of the Territory if:
-- (a) the person is, at the relevant time, not living in the Territory and either: (i) the person has been living outside the
-- Territory for a continuous period of 6 months or more; or (ii) the person's primary dwelling house or primary employment is
-- not in the Territory; or (b) the person has left the Territory with the intention of no longer residing in the Territory."
DECLARE `Residence` HAS
    `had resided in the Territory for a continuous period of at least 3 months`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `was not living in the Territory at the time`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `had been living outside the Territory for a continuous period of 6 months or more` IS A BOOLEAN
    `primary dwelling house or primary employment was not in the Territory`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `had left the Territory intending no longer to reside there`                       IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the residence` IS A `Residence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a resident of the Territory` `the residence` IF
        `the residence`'s `had resided in the Territory for a continuous period of at least 3 months`
    AND (NOT (    (    `the residence`'s `was not living in the Territory at the time`
                   AND (    `the residence`'s `had been living outside the Territory for a continuous period of 6 months or more`
                        OR  `the residence`'s `primary dwelling house or primary employment was not in the Territory`))
              OR  `the residence`'s `had left the Territory intending no longer to reside there`))

§§ `s 7 -- who is entitled to benefits`

-- s 7(1): benefits are payable "to, or in relation to, a person who suffers personal injury or dies in, or as a result of, a motor
-- accident occurring in the Territory". (2): and "to, or in relation to, a resident of the Territory who suffers personal injury or
-- dies in, or as a result of, a motor accident occurring outside the Territory if the accident: (a) occurs in Australia; and
-- (b) is caused by or arises out of the use of a Territory motor vehicle." (3): a person "entitled to statutory benefits under
-- subsection (2) may elect to claim damages or compensation under the law of the jurisdiction in which the accident occurred and,
-- if such a claim is made: ... (b) the claimant's entitlement to statutory benefits ceases".
DECLARE `Accident place` HAS
    `occurred in the Territory`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `occurred in Australia`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `arose out of the use of a Territory motor vehicle`           IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Entitlement answer` IS ONE OF
    `entitled: a motor accident in the Territory (s 7(1))`
    `entitled: a Territory resident, in a motor accident elsewhere in Australia arising out of the use of a Territory motor vehicle (s 7(2))`
    `not entitled: it was not a motor accident (s 4A)`
    `not entitled: the accident happened outside Australia (s 7(2)(a))`
    `not entitled: the accident happened outside the Territory and did not arise out of the use of a Territory motor vehicle (s 7(2)(b))`
    `not entitled: the accident happened outside the Territory and the person was not a resident of the Territory (ss 4B, 7(2))`
    `no longer entitled: a claim for damages or compensation was made in the place of the accident (s 7(3)(b))`

GIVEN `the occurrence` IS AN `Occurrence`
      `the place`      IS AN `Accident place`
      `the residence`  IS A `Residence`
      `a claim was made under the law of the place of the accident` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Entitlement answer`
`the s 7 entitlement for` `the occurrence` `at` `the place` `of a person with` `the residence` `who claimed elsewhere` `a claim was made under the law of the place of the accident` MEANS
    IF NOT `the death or injury results from a motor accident` `the occurrence`
    THEN `not entitled: it was not a motor accident (s 4A)`
    ELSE IF `the place`'s `occurred in the Territory`
         THEN `entitled: a motor accident in the Territory (s 7(1))`
         ELSE IF NOT `the place`'s `occurred in Australia`
              THEN `not entitled: the accident happened outside Australia (s 7(2)(a))`
              ELSE IF NOT `the place`'s `arose out of the use of a Territory motor vehicle`
                   THEN `not entitled: the accident happened outside the Territory and did not arise out of the use of a Territory motor vehicle (s 7(2)(b))`
                   ELSE IF NOT `is a resident of the Territory` `the residence`
                        THEN `not entitled: the accident happened outside the Territory and the person was not a resident of the Territory (ss 4B, 7(2))`
                        ELSE IF `a claim was made under the law of the place of the accident`
                             THEN `no longer entitled: a claim for damages or compensation was made in the place of the accident (s 7(3)(b))`
                             ELSE `entitled: a Territory resident, in a motor accident elsewhere in Australia arising out of the use of a Territory motor vehicle (s 7(2))`

GIVEN `the answer` IS AN `Entitlement answer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is entitled` `the answer` IF
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `entitled: a motor accident in the Territory (s 7(1))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `entitled: a Territory resident, in a motor accident elsewhere in Australia arising out of the use of a Territory motor vehicle (s 7(2))` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 7(3)(c)(ii): "the claimant must reimburse the Commission from damages or compensation (if any) awarded on the claim for the
-- amount of the statutory benefits already paid". READING: "from damages" limits the repayment to what is awarded.
GIVEN `statutory benefits already paid` IS A NUMBER
      `damages or compensation awarded` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 7(3)(c)(ii) reimbursement of` `statutory benefits already paid` `from` `damages or compensation awarded` MEANS
    max 0 (min `statutory benefits already paid` `damages or compensation awarded`)

§§ `Part 3 -- exclusions and reductions (ss 9-11B; regs 4A, 4B, 4M)`

-- Regs 4A(1) and 4M(1) (the same words, for s 9(2) and s 20A(2)): "the prescribed circumstances are that, at the time of the
-- accident, the injured person had a concentration of alcohol: (a) in his or her breath of 0.08 grams or more per 210 litres of
-- exhaled breath; or (b) in his or her blood of 0.08 grams or more per 100 millilitres of blood." (2), (3): a breath analysis under
-- the Traffic Act 1987, or a blood sample taken "within 4 hours of the motor accident", is taken to show the concentration at the
-- time. (4): "the analysis that shows the higher concentration of alcohol is to be used". (5): a person who is required to submit to
-- a breath analysis or provide a blood sample "and fails to do so" is taken to exceed the concentration; (6): "However,
-- subregulation (5) does not apply if the Commission is satisfied that the person had a reasonable excuse". (7): otherwise the
-- Commission "may have regard to any relevant information or evidence" -- READING: its finding is given as the readings.
DECLARE `Alcohol readings` HAS
    `the highest breath alcohol concentration, in grams per 210 litres`                          IS A NUMBER
    `the highest blood alcohol concentration from a sample within 4 hours, in grams per 100 millilitres` IS A NUMBER
    `failed to submit to a breath analysis or provide a blood sample when required`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commission is satisfied there was a reasonable excuse for that failure`                 IS A BOOLEAN

`the prescribed concentration` MEANS 0.08

GIVEN `the readings` IS AN `Alcohol readings`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prescribed alcohol circumstances exist` `the readings` IF
        `the readings`'s `the highest breath alcohol concentration, in grams per 210 litres` AT LEAST `the prescribed concentration`
    OR  `the readings`'s `the highest blood alcohol concentration from a sample within 4 hours, in grams per 100 millilitres` AT LEAST `the prescribed concentration`
    OR  (    `the readings`'s `failed to submit to a breath analysis or provide a blood sample when required`
         AND (NOT `the readings`'s `the Commission is satisfied there was a reasonable excuse for that failure`))

-- One person's conduct and vehicle at the time of the accident, for Part 3. (The injured person, or for Part 5 the qualifying
-- person who died.)
DECLARE `Part 3 facts` HAS
    `the day of the accident`                                                                         IS A DATE
    -- s 9, s 20A(1)
    `was driving a motor vehicle`                                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `was under the influence of alcohol or a drug to the extent of committing a road traffic offence`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the alcohol readings`                                                                            IS AN `Alcohol readings`
    `the Commission is of the opinion that the alcohol or drug contributed to the accident`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is established that the alcohol did not contribute to the accident`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 9A
    `the Commission is of the opinion that the person's conduct contributed to the accident`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `has been found guilty, for that conduct, of manslaughter, an offence of seriously harming or endangering others, or dangerous driving` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 9B, s 20A(3)
    `was engaged in conduct that created a substantial risk of injury to themself and recklessly ignored the risk` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 9C
    `had never held a licence for that class of motor vehicle`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the licence was suspended, other than to enforce a fine or penalty`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the licence had been cancelled`                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the licence had lapsed or expired at least 3 months before the accident`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `was driving in breach of the conditions of the licence`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commission is of the opinion that the vehicle was being driven in an emergency`              IS A BOOLEAN
    -- ss 9D-9G
    `was in a motor vehicle`                                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `was the owner of that motor vehicle`                                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `that vehicle was unregistered and had been for at least 3 months`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `that vehicle was of a kind prescribed by reg 4B`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew or ought to have known that the vehicle was unregistered`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `that vehicle was conditionally registered`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew or ought to have known that the vehicle was conditionally registered`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `that vehicle was being driven in breach of the conditions or restrictions of its registration`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accident involved another motor vehicle that was registered and being driven, or conditionally registered and being driven within its conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 10
    `was criminally responsible for the theft or unlawful use of a motor vehicle involved`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `was using a motor vehicle involved for, or in connection with, an indictable offence`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `was using a motor vehicle involved to escape from an offence or to avoid apprehension or detention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was using a motor vehicle involved intending to inflict death or injury on themself or another`   IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 10A
    `the injury or death is compensable under workers compensation legislation, or would be but for self-infliction or serious and wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 10B
    `a motor vehicle involved was taking part in a motor sport event`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `was its driver or passenger, or an official or organiser of the event, or assisting or otherwise associated with it` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 10C
    `it is reasonable to characterise the accident as a terrorist act`                                IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 9(1): not entitled to the s 9 benefits if "(a) the accident occurred while the person was driving a motor vehicle; and (b) the
-- person was under the influence of alcohol or a drug to such an extent that the person: (i) was, by driving a motor vehicle,
-- committing an offence against relevant laws regulating road traffic; or (ii) would have been committing such an offence if the
-- person had been driving the motor vehicle in a public street or public place; and (c) the influence of the alcohol or drug
-- contributed, in the Commission's opinion, to the accident." (2): "The Commission must presume that the influence of alcohol
-- contributed to the accident if the circumstances prescribed in the regulations exist in relation to the person, unless the
-- contrary is established." (3): the benefits are "(a) compensation for loss of earning capacity; and (b) lump sum compensation for
-- a permanent impairment". The presumption reaches (c) only; (b) is still a fact.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the influence of alcohol or a drug contributed to the accident` `the facts` IF
    IF `the prescribed alcohol circumstances exist` (`the facts`'s `the alcohol readings`)
    THEN NOT `the facts`'s `it is established that the alcohol did not contribute to the accident`
    ELSE `the facts`'s `the Commission is of the opinion that the alcohol or drug contributed to the accident`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9 applies` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `was driving a motor vehicle`
    AND `the facts`'s `was under the influence of alcohol or a drug to the extent of committing a road traffic offence`
    AND `the influence of alcohol or a drug contributed to the accident` `the facts`

-- s 9A(1): "(a) the injured person's conduct contributed, in the Commission's opinion, to the accident; and (b) the injured person
-- has been found guilty in respect of that conduct ... of: (i) manslaughter; or (ii) an offence of which an element is an
-- intentional, reckless or criminally negligent act or omission that causes serious harm to, or endangers the life, health or
-- safety of, another or others; or (iii) an offence of which an element is dangerous driving."
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9A applies` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `the Commission is of the opinion that the person's conduct contributed to the accident`
    AND `the facts`'s `has been found guilty, for that conduct, of manslaughter, an offence of seriously harming or endangering others, or dangerous driving`

-- s 9B(1): "(a) the accident occurred while the injured person was engaged in conduct that created a substantial risk of injury to
-- the injured person; and (b) the injured person recklessly ignored the risk." (3): "This section does not apply in relation to
-- conduct mentioned in section 11(1)(c)" (not wearing a seat belt or helmet): the input leaves that conduct out.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9B applies` `the facts` IF
    `the facts`'s `was engaged in conduct that created a substantial risk of injury to themself and recklessly ignored the risk`

-- s 9C(1): "(a) the accident occurred while the injured person was driving a motor vehicle; and (b) one of the following applies:
-- (i) ... never held a licence ... of the relevant class ...; (ii) ... under suspension (for reasons other than for the enforcement
-- of a fine or penalty); (iii) ... cancelled; (iv) ... lapsed or expired at least 3 months before the date of the motor accident;
-- (v) ... driving the motor vehicle in breach of conditions". (2): "does not apply if, in the opinion of the Commission, the
-- circumstances in which the vehicle was being driven amounted to an emergency."
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9C applies` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `was driving a motor vehicle`
    AND (    `the facts`'s `had never held a licence for that class of motor vehicle`
         OR  `the facts`'s `the licence was suspended, other than to enforce a fine or penalty`
         OR  `the facts`'s `the licence had been cancelled`
         OR  `the facts`'s `the licence had lapsed or expired at least 3 months before the accident`
         OR  `the facts`'s `was driving in breach of the conditions of the licence`)
    AND (NOT `the facts`'s `the Commission is of the opinion that the vehicle was being driven in an emergency`)

-- ss 9D(1)(a)-(d) and 9E(1)(a)-(d): "(a) the accident occurred while the injured person was in a motor vehicle; and (b) the motor
-- vehicle was unregistered and had been unregistered for a period of at least 3 months; and (c) the injured person was the owner
-- or driver of the motor vehicle; and (d) if the injured person was the driver of the motor vehicle: (i) the motor vehicle was of
-- a kind prescribed by regulation; or (ii) otherwise -- the driver knew, or ought to have known, the vehicle was unregistered".
-- The knowledge test in (d) is for a driver only: an owner who was a passenger needs none (finding 8).
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unregistered vehicle conditions in ss 9D and 9E are met` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `was in a motor vehicle`
    AND `the facts`'s `that vehicle was unregistered and had been for at least 3 months`
    AND (`the facts`'s `was the owner of that motor vehicle` OR `the facts`'s `was driving a motor vehicle`)
    AND (    (NOT `the facts`'s `was driving a motor vehicle`)
         OR  `the facts`'s `that vehicle was of a kind prescribed by reg 4B`
         OR  `the facts`'s `knew or ought to have known that the vehicle was unregistered`)

-- s 9D(1)(e): "the accident involved another motor vehicle that was either: (i) a registered motor vehicle that, at the time of the
-- accident, was being driven; or (ii) a conditionally registered motor vehicle that ... was being driven in compliance with the
-- conditions or restrictions on which the vehicle was registered." (2): the emergency exception. (3): "The benefits to which this
-- section applies are all benefits payable under this Act other than those payable under sections 18, 18BC, 18BD and 19."
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9D applies` `the facts` IF
        `the unregistered vehicle conditions in ss 9D and 9E are met` `the facts`
    AND `the facts`'s `the accident involved another motor vehicle that was registered and being driven, or conditionally registered and being driven within its conditions`
    AND (NOT `the facts`'s `the Commission is of the opinion that the vehicle was being driven in an emergency`)

-- s 9E(1): "No benefits are payable under this Act" if (a)-(d) and "(e) section 9D does not apply"; (2): the emergency exception.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9E applies` `the facts` IF
        `the unregistered vehicle conditions in ss 9D and 9E are met` `the facts`
    AND (NOT `s 9D applies` `the facts`)
    AND (NOT `the facts`'s `the Commission is of the opinion that the vehicle was being driven in an emergency`)

-- ss 9F(1)(a)-(d) and 9G(1)(a)-(d): "(a) ... in a motor vehicle; and (b) the motor vehicle was conditionally registered; and (c) the
-- injured person: (i) was the owner of the conditionally registered motor vehicle; or (ii) was the driver of the conditionally
-- registered motor vehicle and knew, or ought to have known, that the vehicle was conditionally registered; and (d) the vehicle
-- was driven in breach of the conditions or restrictions on which the vehicle was registered".
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conditional registration conditions in ss 9F and 9G are met` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `was in a motor vehicle`
    AND `the facts`'s `that vehicle was conditionally registered`
    AND (    `the facts`'s `was the owner of that motor vehicle`
         OR  (`the facts`'s `was driving a motor vehicle` AND `the facts`'s `knew or ought to have known that the vehicle was conditionally registered`))
    AND `the facts`'s `that vehicle was being driven in breach of the conditions or restrictions of its registration`

-- s 9F: as s 9D, with the conditionally registered vehicle; (3): all benefits other than under ss 18, 18BC, 18BD and 19.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9F applies` `the facts` IF
        `the conditional registration conditions in ss 9F and 9G are met` `the facts`
    AND `the facts`'s `the accident involved another motor vehicle that was registered and being driven, or conditionally registered and being driven within its conditions`
    AND (NOT `the facts`'s `the Commission is of the opinion that the vehicle was being driven in an emergency`)

-- s 9G: "No benefits are payable" if (a)-(d) and "(e) section 9F does not apply"; (2): the emergency exception.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9G applies` `the facts` IF
        `the conditional registration conditions in ss 9F and 9G are met` `the facts`
    AND (NOT `s 9F applies` `the facts`)
    AND (NOT `the facts`'s `the Commission is of the opinion that the vehicle was being driven in an emergency`)

-- s 10: "No benefits are payable under this Act ... if the person: (a) was ... criminally responsible for the theft or unlawful use
-- of a motor vehicle involved in the accident (whether or not the person's guilt has been established in criminal proceedings); or
-- (b) was using a motor vehicle involved in the accident for, or in connection with, the commission of an indictable offence ...;
-- or (c) was using a motor vehicle involved in the accident to escape from the scene of, or to avoid apprehension or escape
-- detention for, an offence ...; or (d) was using a motor vehicle involved in the accident intending to inflict death or injury on
-- himself, herself or another."
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10 applies` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `was criminally responsible for the theft or unlawful use of a motor vehicle involved`
    OR  `the facts`'s `was using a motor vehicle involved for, or in connection with, an indictable offence`
    OR  `the facts`'s `was using a motor vehicle involved to escape from an offence or to avoid apprehension or detention`
    OR  `the facts`'s `was using a motor vehicle involved intending to inflict death or injury on themself or another`

-- s 10A: "No benefits are payable ... if the injury or death: (a) is compensable under workers compensation legislation; or (b) would
-- have been so compensable but for the fact that the person's injury or death: (i) was deliberately self-inflicted; or (ii) is
-- attributable to the person's serious and wilful misconduct." s 4: "workers compensation legislation means the Return to Work Act
-- 1986 or the corresponding legislation of another jurisdiction." Whether it is compensable is answered under that Act: an INPUT.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10A applies` `the facts` IF
    `the facts`'s `the injury or death is compensable under workers compensation legislation, or would be but for self-infliction or serious and wilful misconduct`

-- s 10B(1): "No benefits are payable ... if a motor vehicle involved in the accident was taking part in a motor sport event, and at
-- the time of the motor accident the injured person was: (a) the driver of, or a passenger in, the motor vehicle; or (b) an official
-- or organiser of the event; or (c) assisting in any way in the holding of the event; or (d) assisting participants in the event;
-- or (e) otherwise associated with the holding of the event."
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10B applies` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `a motor vehicle involved was taking part in a motor sport event`
    AND `the facts`'s `was its driver or passenger, or an official or organiser of the event, or assisting or otherwise associated with it`

-- s 10C(1): "No benefits are payable ... if, having regard to the nature of the accident and the context in which the accident
-- occurred, it is reasonable to characterise the accident as a terrorist act."
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10C applies` `the facts` IF
    `the facts`'s `it is reasonable to characterise the accident as a terrorist act`

-- s 11B: "If 2 or more of the exclusions or reductions under this Part apply in relation to an injury or death, those provisions
-- apply cumulatively." So the widest exclusion governs, and every provision that applies is listed.
DECLARE `Part 3 exclusion` IS ONE OF
    `no benefits are payable at all` HAS `under` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `only medical and rehabilitation, long-term and interim attendant care and appliance benefits are payable` HAS `under` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `no compensation for loss of earning capacity and no lump sum for permanent impairment` HAS `under` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `no exclusion applies`
    `outside this encoding: the accident happened before 1 July 2014, and Part 3 as it stood before the 2014 amendments is not deposited (s 46)`

GIVEN `applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the section` IS A STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`listed if` `applies` `as` `the section` MEANS
    IF `applies` THEN LIST `the section` ELSE EMPTY

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the total exclusions that apply to` `the facts` MEANS
    concat (LIST (`listed if` (`s 9E applies` `the facts`) `as` "s 9E"),
                 (`listed if` (`s 9G applies` `the facts`) `as` "s 9G"),
                 (`listed if` (`s 10 applies` `the facts`) `as` "s 10"),
                 (`listed if` (`s 10A applies` `the facts`) `as` "s 10A"),
                 (`listed if` (`s 10B applies` `the facts`) `as` "s 10B"),
                 (`listed if` (`s 10C applies` `the facts`) `as` "s 10C"))

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the registration exclusions that apply to` `the facts` MEANS
    concat (LIST (`listed if` (`s 9D applies` `the facts`) `as` "s 9D"),
                 (`listed if` (`s 9F applies` `the facts`) `as` "s 9F"))

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the earning capacity and impairment exclusions that apply to` `the facts` MEANS
    concat (LIST (`listed if` (`s 9 applies` `the facts`) `as` "s 9"),
                 (`listed if` (`s 9A applies` `the facts`) `as` "s 9A"),
                 (`listed if` (`s 9B applies` `the facts`) `as` "s 9B"),
                 (`listed if` (`s 9C applies` `the facts`) `as` "s 9C"))

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A `Part 3 exclusion`
`the Part 3 exclusion for` `the facts` MEANS
    IF `the facts`'s `the day of the accident` `is before` `the 2014 amendments commenced`
    THEN `outside this encoding: the accident happened before 1 July 2014, and Part 3 as it stood before the 2014 amendments is not deposited (s 46)`
    ELSE IF NOT null `the total`
         THEN `no benefits are payable at all` `all that apply`
         ELSE IF NOT null `the registration ones`
              THEN `only medical and rehabilitation, long-term and interim attendant care and appliance benefits are payable` `all that apply`
              ELSE IF NOT null `the earning capacity ones`
                   THEN `no compensation for loss of earning capacity and no lump sum for permanent impairment` `all that apply`
                   ELSE `no exclusion applies`
    WHERE
        `the total` MEANS `the total exclusions that apply to` `the facts`
        `the registration ones` MEANS `the registration exclusions that apply to` `the facts`
        `the earning capacity ones` MEANS `the earning capacity and impairment exclusions that apply to` `the facts`
        `all that apply` MEANS concat (LIST `the earning capacity ones`, `the registration ones`, `the total`)

-- s 11(1): applies if a person "(a) is injured or dies in, or as a result of, a motor accident; and (b) was, at the time of the
-- accident, of or above the age of 16 years; and (c) was not wearing a seat belt or safety helmet as required under the Traffic Act
-- 1987 (or ... the corresponding law of the relevant jurisdiction)." The note: it "applies only to an illegal failure" and not with an
-- exemption under the Motor Vehicles Act 1949. (2): the benefits "are reduced by 25% of the amount otherwise payable". (3): "(a)
-- compensation for loss of earning capacity; and (b) lump sum compensation for a permanent impairment; and (c) compensation under
-- sections 22 and 23 for a death or dependency." Not s 24 (finding 13).
GIVEN `age at the accident` IS A NUMBER
      `was not wearing a seat belt or safety helmet as the law required` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 11 applies to a person of` `age at the accident` `who` `was not wearing a seat belt or safety helmet as the law required` IF
        `age at the accident` AT LEAST 16
    AND `was not wearing a seat belt or safety helmet as the law required`

`the s 11 reduction` MEANS 25%

-- Apply s 11 (a proportion of the amount otherwise payable) and then s 11A ("reduced by the amount of the entitlement to insurance
-- or compensation that arises, apart from this Act"). READING (finding 12): s 11B makes them cumulative without an order; s 11 is
-- taken first, as a share of the amount the benefit section gives, and s 11A then takes away an amount, never below nil. How an
-- s 11A entitlement is spread across several benefits is not said: the amount set against each benefit is an INPUT.
GIVEN `the amount otherwise payable` IS A NUMBER
      `s 11 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the s 11A entitlement set against it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`after ss 11 and 11A,` `the amount otherwise payable` `with s 11` `s 11 applies` `less` `the s 11A entitlement set against it` MEANS
    max 0 (`after s 11` MINUS `the s 11A entitlement set against it`)
    WHERE
        `after s 11` MEANS
            IF `s 11 applies`
            THEN `the amount otherwise payable` MINUS (`the amount otherwise payable` TIMES `the s 11 reduction`)
            ELSE `the amount otherwise payable`

§§ `s 13 -- compensation for loss of earning capacity`

-- s 13(5)(a): "a person stops being entitled to benefits under this section: (i) if the day of the accident is more than 2 years
-- before the day the person reaches pension age -- on the day the person reaches pension age; or (ii) otherwise -- 104 weeks after the
-- day of the accident". (7): "pension age, see section 23(1) of the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth)": an INPUT, the day.
-- READING: "more than 2 years before" is compared on the calendar: the accident's day two years on falls before the pension-age day.
`104 weeks in days` MEANS 728

GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE
      `the day pension age is reached` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the s 13 entitlement stops, for an accident on` `the day of the accident` `and pension age on` `the day pension age is reached` MEANS
    IF ((`the calendar key of` `the day of the accident`) PLUS 20000) LESS THAN `the calendar key of` `the day pension age is reached`
    THEN `the day pension age is reached`
    ELSE `the day` `104 weeks in days` `days after` `the day of the accident`

-- s 14(1): a person who "at the time of the relevant accident: (a) had not attained the age of 15 years; or (b) had attained that age
-- but was a full-time student at a school, college or university: (i) there being, in the opinion of the Commission, no substantial
-- break in the continuation of the person studies; (ii) who was not married or in a relationship that ... was a de facto
-- relationship; and (iii) whose earnings from personal exertion ... in the 3 months to that time did not exceed 25% of ... the average
-- earnings during that period of wage earners in the Territory, shall not receive a benefit under that section except in respect of a
-- period commencing on the date on which: (c) the person attains the age of 15 years; or (d) the person ceases to be a full-time
-- student or sooner marries or enters a relationship that ... is a de facto relationship, whichever is the later", and is then
-- "deemed to have suffered a reduction in earning capacity". READING: a child under 15 who was not a full-time student has nothing
-- to cease, so (d) is met at the accident.
DECLARE `Young person` HAS
    `the date of birth`                                                                              IS A DATE
    `was a full-time student at the accident, with no substantial break in study`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `was married or in a de facto relationship at the accident`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `earned no more than 25% of average Territory wage earners' earnings in the 3 months before`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `has since stopped full-time study, or sooner married or entered a de facto relationship`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day full-time study stopped, or of the marriage or de facto relationship if sooner`          IS A DATE
    `by the week in question has married, entered a de facto relationship or had someone become primarily dependent on them` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `s 14(1) start` IS ONE OF
    `s 14(1) does not apply`
    `benefits may be paid only from` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `benefits wait until full-time study stops, or marriage or a de facto relationship`

GIVEN `the person` IS A `Young person`
      `the day of the accident` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `s 14(1) start`
`the s 14(1) start for` `the person` `injured on` `the day of the accident` MEANS
    IF `the age at the accident` LESS THAN 15
    THEN IF `the person`'s `was a full-time student at the accident, with no substantial break in study`
         THEN `the later start`
         ELSE `benefits may be paid only from` `the fifteenth birthday`
    ELSE IF     `the person`'s `was a full-time student at the accident, with no substantial break in study`
            AND (NOT `the person`'s `was married or in a de facto relationship at the accident`)
            AND `the person`'s `earned no more than 25% of average Territory wage earners' earnings in the 3 months before`
         THEN `the later start`
         ELSE `s 14(1) does not apply`
    WHERE
        `the age at the accident` MEANS `the age of a person born` (`the person`'s `the date of birth`) `on` `the day of the accident`
        `the fifteenth birthday` MEANS `the day` 180 `months after` (`the person`'s `the date of birth`)
        `the later start` MEANS
            IF `the person`'s `has since stopped full-time study, or sooner married or entered a de facto relationship`
            THEN `benefits may be paid only from` (`the later of` `the fifteenth birthday` `and` (`the person`'s `the day full-time study stopped, or of the marriage or de facto relationship if sooner`))
            ELSE `benefits wait until full-time study stops, or marriage or a de facto relationship`

-- s 14(2): for a person "who has not attained the age of 21 years and is not married", the "relevant percentage" for the age the
-- person "remains of": "| 15 | 40 |", "| 16 | 55 |", "| 17 | 60 |", "| 18 | 70 |", "| 19 | 80 |", "| 20 | 90 |". (3): a person who
-- "(a) marries; or (b) enters a relationship that ... is a de facto relationship; or (c) has a child or other person primarily dependent
-- on the person for financial support" gets "the full amount ... in respect of the period commencing on the date" of it.
-- The table reaches every unmarried recipient under 21, not only the s 14(1) students (finding 10).
GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER
      `married, de facto or with a dependant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 14 percentage at age` `the age` `if` `married, de facto or with a dependant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `married, de facto or with a dependant` OR `the age` AT LEAST 21 THEN 100%
        IF `the age` EQUALS 20 THEN 90%
        IF `the age` EQUALS 19 THEN 80%
        IF `the age` EQUALS 18 THEN 70%
        IF `the age` EQUALS 17 THEN 60%
        IF `the age` EQUALS 16 THEN 55%
        IF `the age` EQUALS 15 THEN 40%
        OTHERWISE 0

-- One week of a claim for loss of earning capacity.
DECLARE `Earning capacity week` HAS
    `the day of the accident`                                                                         IS A DATE
    `the first day of the week`                                                                       IS A DATE
    `the day pension age is reached`                                                                  IS A DATE
    `the young person`                                                                                IS A `Young person`
    `the Commission considers the capacity to earn from personal exertion reduced by the injury`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `earned income from personal exertion on the day of the accident, as the Commission is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the maximum amount MA for the half-year`                                                         IS A NUMBER
    `the Commission determined the person capable of full-time work that week`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `earnings from work that week`                                                                    IS A NUMBER
    `the weekly amount the Commission calculated under s 13(3)`                                        IS A NUMBER
    `was detained in a penal institution throughout the week`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `was outside Australia throughout the week`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `was not wearing a seat belt or safety helmet as the law required`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the s 11A entitlement set against the week`                                                       IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Nil week reason` IS ONE OF
    `the Commission does not consider the capacity to earn reduced by the injury (s 13(1))`
    `pension age or older at the accident, and not someone who earned income from personal exertion (s 13(5A))`
    `the Commission determined the person capable of full-time work that week (s 13(2)(b)(ii))`
    `earnings that week were at least the maximum amount (s 13(2)(b)(iii))`
    `detained in a penal institution (s 13(5)(b))`
    `outside Australia (s 13(5)(c))`

DECLARE `Weekly benefit answer` IS ONE OF
    `the weekly benefit, in dollars, is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `nothing is payable for that week` HAS `because` IS A `Nil week reason`
    `not yet payable: s 14(1) defers it until` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `not yet payable: s 14(1) defers it until full-time study stops, or marriage or a de facto relationship`
    `the entitlement stopped (s 13(5)(a)) on` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `outside this encoding: the accident happened before 31 May 2019, and s 13 as it stood before the 2019 amendments is not deposited (s 49)`
    `outside this encoding: the week includes the day of the accident or the day the entitlement stops, and the Act does not say how a part week is paid`

-- s 13(1): payable "if an eligible person's capacity to earn income from personal exertion ... is, in the opinion of the Commission,
-- reduced as a result of an injury". (2)(a): "the maximum amount payable per week is the amount determined by the Commission, for
-- each 6 month period commencing on 1 January or 1 July, to be 85% of the average weekly earnings for all employees' total
-- employment earnings in the Territory ... less a notional deduction for income tax" (MA: an INPUT; (2A) disapplies the s 4
-- definition). (2)(b): "compensation is not payable ... for any of the following periods: (i) the day of the accident; (ii) any weekly
-- period that the Commission determines the person is capable of working full-time, regardless of the type of work; (iii) any weekly
-- period that the Commission determines the person earned a sum equal to or exceeding the maximum amount". (2)(c), (3): the amount by
-- the lost formula, "MA is the maximum amount" (an INPUT bounded by MA). (2)(d): "to be paid without any deduction for income tax".
-- (5)(b): "not entitled ... while detained in a penal institution (within or outside the Territory)"; (c): "while outside Australia".
-- (5A): "if the person ... is pension age or older on the day of the accident, compensation is not payable ... unless the Commission
-- is satisfied that, on the day of the accident, the person was someone who earns income from personal exertion."
GIVEN `the week` IS AN `Earning capacity week`
GIVETH A `Weekly benefit answer`
`the s 13 weekly benefit for` `the week` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the week`'s `the day of the accident` `is before` `the 2019 amendments commenced`
        THEN `outside this encoding: the accident happened before 31 May 2019, and s 13 as it stood before the 2019 amendments is not deposited (s 49)`
        IF NOT `the week`'s `the day of the accident` `is before` `the week`'s `the first day of the week`
        THEN `outside this encoding: the week includes the day of the accident or the day the entitlement stops, and the Act does not say how a part week is paid`
        IF `the week`'s `the first day of the week` `is on or after` `the stop day`
        THEN `the entitlement stopped (s 13(5)(a)) on` `the stop day`
        IF `the last day of the week` `is on or after` `the stop day`
        THEN `outside this encoding: the week includes the day of the accident or the day the entitlement stops, and the Act does not say how a part week is paid`
        IF     (`the week`'s `the day of the accident` `is on or after` `the week`'s `the day pension age is reached`)
           AND (NOT `the week`'s `earned income from personal exertion on the day of the accident, as the Commission is satisfied`)
        THEN `nothing is payable for that week` `pension age or older at the accident, and not someone who earned income from personal exertion (s 13(5A))`
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the s 14(1) start for` (`the week`'s `the young person`) `injured on` (`the week`'s `the day of the accident`)
            WHEN `benefits wait until full-time study stops, or marriage or a de facto relationship` THEN `not yet payable: s 14(1) defers it until full-time study stops, or marriage or a de facto relationship`
            WHEN `benefits may be paid only from` `the start` THEN
                IF `the week`'s `the first day of the week` `is before` `the start`
                THEN `not yet payable: s 14(1) defers it until` `the start`
                ELSE `the payable week` TRUE
            WHEN `s 14(1) does not apply` THEN `the payable week` FALSE
    WHERE
        `the stop day` MEANS `the day the s 13 entitlement stops, for an accident on` (`the week`'s `the day of the accident`) `and pension age on` (`the week`'s `the day pension age is reached`)
        `the last day of the week` MEANS `the day` 6 `days after` (`the week`'s `the first day of the week`)
        `the age that week` MEANS `the age of a person born` (`the week`'s `the young person`'s `the date of birth`) `on` (`the week`'s `the first day of the week`)
        `the age at the accident` MEANS `the age of a person born` (`the week`'s `the young person`'s `the date of birth`) `on` (`the week`'s `the day of the accident`)
        `MA` MEANS `the week`'s `the maximum amount MA for the half-year`
        GIVEN `deemed` IS A BOOLEAN
        GIVETH A `Weekly benefit answer`
        `the payable week` `deemed` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF (NOT `deemed`) AND (NOT `the week`'s `the Commission considers the capacity to earn from personal exertion reduced by the injury`)
                THEN `nothing is payable for that week` `the Commission does not consider the capacity to earn reduced by the injury (s 13(1))`
                IF `the week`'s `was detained in a penal institution throughout the week`
                THEN `nothing is payable for that week` `detained in a penal institution (s 13(5)(b))`
                IF `the week`'s `was outside Australia throughout the week`
                THEN `nothing is payable for that week` `outside Australia (s 13(5)(c))`
                IF `the week`'s `the Commission determined the person capable of full-time work that week`
                THEN `nothing is payable for that week` `the Commission determined the person capable of full-time work that week (s 13(2)(b)(ii))`
                IF `the week`'s `earnings from work that week` AT LEAST `MA`
                THEN `nothing is payable for that week` `earnings that week were at least the maximum amount (s 13(2)(b)(iii))`
                OTHERWISE `the weekly benefit, in dollars, is` (`after ss 11 and 11A,` `the s 14 amount` `with s 11` (`s 11 applies to a person of` `the age at the accident` `who` (`the week`'s `was not wearing a seat belt or safety helmet as the law required`)) `less` (`the week`'s `the s 11A entitlement set against the week`))
        `the s 14 amount` MEANS
            (min (`the week`'s `the weekly amount the Commission calculated under s 13(3)`) `MA`) TIMES (`the s 14 percentage at age` `the age that week` `if` (`the week`'s `the young person`'s `by the week in question has married, entered a de facto relationship or had someone become primarily dependent on them`))

§§ `s 17 -- lump sum for permanent impairment (ss 4C, 17; reg 4)`

-- s 4C(1)-(3): whether an impairment is permanent, and its extent, "is to be determined by the Commission ... in accordance with the
-- edition of the American Medical Association Guides to the Evaluation of Permanent Impairment prescribed by regulation" and "on the
-- advice of a medical practitioner", "expressed as a percentage of the whole person". Reg 4(1): "the American Medical Association Guides
-- to the Evaluation of Permanent Impairment, 6th Edition is prescribed." The percentage is the Commission's: an INPUT. (4): "not
-- considered to be a permanent impairment unless the extent ... is at least 5%".
-- s 17(1A): "the assessed percentage of the prescribed amount". (2): for "5% or more but less than 15% as shown in Column 1", the
-- percentage in Column 2: "| not less than 5% but less than 10% | 2 |", "| 10% | 3 |", "| 11% | 4 |", "| 12% | 6 |", "| 13% | 8 |",
-- "| 14% | 12 |". (3): "prescribed amount, in relation to a payment, means 208 times average weekly earnings at the time the payment
-- is made." A percentage between the whole-number rows (10.5%) is in no row (finding 6): `outside this encoding`.
DECLARE `Table percentage` IS ONE OF
    `the percentage of the prescribed amount is` HAS `percent` IS A NUMBER
    `below the 5% threshold`
    `between the rows of the s 17(2) table`

GIVEN `the assessed percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Table percentage`
`the s 17 percentage of the prescribed amount for` `the assessed percentage` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the assessed percentage` LESS THAN 5 THEN `below the 5% threshold`
        IF `the assessed percentage` LESS THAN 10 THEN `the percentage of the prescribed amount is` 2
        IF `the assessed percentage` EQUALS 10 THEN `the percentage of the prescribed amount is` 3
        IF `the assessed percentage` EQUALS 11 THEN `the percentage of the prescribed amount is` 4
        IF `the assessed percentage` EQUALS 12 THEN `the percentage of the prescribed amount is` 6
        IF `the assessed percentage` EQUALS 13 THEN `the percentage of the prescribed amount is` 8
        IF `the assessed percentage` EQUALS 14 THEN `the percentage of the prescribed amount is` 12
        IF `the assessed percentage` LESS THAN 15 THEN `between the rows of the s 17(2) table`
        OTHERWISE `the percentage of the prescribed amount is` (min 100 `the assessed percentage`)

`the prescribed amount multiple` MEANS 208

DECLARE `Impairment claim` HAS
    `the assessed percentage of permanent impairment of the whole person`        IS A NUMBER
    `average weekly earnings when the payment is made`                         IS A NUMBER
    `is in Australia when the payment is made`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `a lump sum on an assessment of this impairment has already been paid`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 11 applies`                                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the s 11A entitlement set against it`                                     IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `No lump sum reason` IS ONE OF
    `the impairment is assessed at less than 5% (ss 4C(4), 17(1)(b))`
    `a lump sum on an assessment of this impairment has already been paid (s 17(4))`
    `not in Australia when the payment is made (s 17(5))`

DECLARE `Impairment lump sum answer` IS ONE OF
    `the lump sum, in dollars, is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no lump sum` HAS `because` IS A `No lump sum reason`
    `outside this encoding: the assessed percentage falls between the whole-number rows of the s 17(2) table`

-- s 17(4): "After compensation based on an assessment of the extent of a permanent impairment has been paid, no further right to
-- compensation under this section arises even though the extent of the impairment later increases." (5): "may only be paid ... to,
-- or for the benefit of, a person who is, at the time of the payment, in Australia."
GIVEN `the claim` IS AN `Impairment claim`
GIVETH AN `Impairment lump sum answer`
`the s 17 lump sum for` `the claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the s 17 percentage of the prescribed amount for` (`the claim`'s `the assessed percentage of permanent impairment of the whole person`)
    WHEN `below the 5% threshold` THEN `no lump sum` `the impairment is assessed at less than 5% (ss 4C(4), 17(1)(b))`
    WHEN `between the rows of the s 17(2) table` THEN `outside this encoding: the assessed percentage falls between the whole-number rows of the s 17(2) table`
    WHEN `the percentage of the prescribed amount is` `percent` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `the claim`'s `a lump sum on an assessment of this impairment has already been paid`
            THEN `no lump sum` `a lump sum on an assessment of this impairment has already been paid (s 17(4))`
            IF NOT `the claim`'s `is in Australia when the payment is made`
            THEN `no lump sum` `not in Australia when the payment is made (s 17(5))`
            OTHERWISE `the lump sum, in dollars, is` (`after ss 11 and 11A,` ((`percent` DIVIDED BY 100) TIMES `the prescribed amount`) `with s 11` (`the claim`'s `s 11 applies`) `less` (`the claim`'s `the s 11A entitlement set against it`))
    WHERE
        `the prescribed amount` MEANS `the prescribed amount multiple` TIMES (`the claim`'s `average weekly earnings when the payment is made`)

§§ `s 18 -- medical and rehabilitation services (reg 4D)`

-- s 18(1): "Compensation is payable under this section for the reasonable cost of medical and rehabilitation services that are
-- necessary and reasonably required by an eligible person as a result of an injury arising from the motor accident." (2): "(a)
-- medical, surgical and dental treatment; and (b) nursing and other professional care (not including attendant care services); and
-- (c) training and education (not including attendant care services) for rehabilitation ...; and (d) conveying the person to and
-- from a hospital or other place for treatment ...; and (e) hospitalisation, or accommodation in some other institution". (5): "No
-- compensation is to be paid under this section for: (a) attendant care services; or (b) services provided outside Australia."
-- Reg 4D: in deciding whether services are "reasonable and necessary" the Commission "must consider" the listed matters: its
-- judgment, an INPUT.
DECLARE `Medical service` HAS
    `the day of the accident`                                                     IS A DATE
    `is a medical and rehabilitation service listed in s 18(2)`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an attendant care service (personal or household services)`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `is provided outside Australia`                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `is required as a result of the injury`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commission considers it necessary and reasonable, having considered reg 4D` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Medical answer` IS ONE OF
    `covered: the reasonable cost is payable (s 18(1))`
    `not covered: attendant care services are not paid under s 18 (s 18(5)(a))`
    `not covered: services provided outside Australia (s 18(5)(b))`
    `not covered: not a medical and rehabilitation service (s 18(2))`
    `not covered: not required as a result of the injury (s 18(1))`
    `not covered: the Commission does not consider it necessary and reasonable (s 18(1), reg 4D)`
    `outside this encoding: the accident happened before 1 July 2014, and s 18 as it stood before the 2014 amendments is not deposited (s 47)`

GIVEN `the service` IS A `Medical service`
GIVETH A `Medical answer`
`the s 18 answer for` `the service` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the service`'s `the day of the accident` `is before` `the 2014 amendments commenced`
        THEN `outside this encoding: the accident happened before 1 July 2014, and s 18 as it stood before the 2014 amendments is not deposited (s 47)`
        IF `the service`'s `is an attendant care service (personal or household services)`
        THEN `not covered: attendant care services are not paid under s 18 (s 18(5)(a))`
        IF NOT `the service`'s `is a medical and rehabilitation service listed in s 18(2)`
        THEN `not covered: not a medical and rehabilitation service (s 18(2))`
        IF `the service`'s `is provided outside Australia`
        THEN `not covered: services provided outside Australia (s 18(5)(b))`
        IF NOT `the service`'s `is required as a result of the injury`
        THEN `not covered: not required as a result of the injury (s 18(1))`
        IF NOT `the service`'s `the Commission considers it necessary and reasonable, having considered reg 4D`
        THEN `not covered: the Commission does not consider it necessary and reasonable (s 18(1), reg 4D)`
        OTHERWISE `covered: the reasonable cost is payable (s 18(1))`

§§ `ss 18BA-18BE -- attendant care eligibility, injuries on or after 1 July 2014 (regs 4E, 4F)`

-- s 18BB(1): short-term benefits if the person "(a) ... suffers an impairment as a result of the injury ...; and (b) ... requires
-- attendant care services in consequence of the impairment; and (c) ... has not been assessed as eligible for interim or long-term
-- attendant care services." (2): "payable for a period of up to 1 year after the date of the motor accident."
-- s 18BC(1): long-term benefits on (a), (b) and "(c) the criteria prescribed by regulation"; (2): "payable for life". Reg 4E: "(a) the
-- person has suffered an injury of a kind listed in Schedule 1; and (b) either subregulation (2) or (3) applies"; (2): "(a) the
-- criteria set out in Schedule 1 for that kind of injury are satisfied; and (b) the injury is permanent and stable"; (3): if (2) does
-- not apply but "in the opinion of the Commission, exceptional circumstances exist ... which warrant the payment".
-- s 18BD(1): interim benefits on (a), (b) and the reg 4F criteria; reg 4F(2): "(a) the criteria set out in Schedule 1 for the injury
-- (excluding any requirements as to the permanency of the injury) are satisfied; and (b) the person's condition at the date of
-- assessment is not permanent and stable"; (3): exceptional circumstances. 18BD(2): "not payable if benefits are payable under
-- section 18BC". (3): they "cease to be payable: (a) if the injured person was less than 3 years of age at the date of the accident --
-- when the person attains 6 years of age; or (b) otherwise -- 3 years after the date the injured person makes a claim". (5): not
-- "more than once for the same impairment". s 18BE(1): only for services "(a) ... provided in Australia; and (b) in the opinion of the
-- Commission: (i) ... necessary and reasonable ...; and (ii) relate to the person's injury; and (c) ... of a standard the Commission
-- considers appropriate; and (d) ... provided by: (i) an approved provider; or (ii) ... a person approved by the Commission".
-- Schedule 1 (the injuries and their criteria) is assessed by a medical specialist's certificate (regs 4E(4), 4F(4)): INPUTS.
DECLARE `Attendant care facts` HAS
    `the day of the accident`                                                                 IS A DATE
    `the date of birth`                                                                       IS A DATE
    `the day the claim was made`                                                              IS A DATE
    `suffers an impairment as a result of the injury`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `requires attendant care services in consequence of the impairment`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `has an injury of a kind listed in Schedule 1`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `meets the Schedule 1 criteria for that injury in full`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `meets the Schedule 1 criteria for that injury, leaving aside any requirement of permanency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injury is permanent and stable`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commission considers exceptional circumstances warrant long-term benefits`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commission considers exceptional circumstances warrant interim benefits`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `has already had interim benefits for the same impairment`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the services meet s 18BE`                                                                IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Attendant care answer` IS ONE OF
    `long-term attendant care benefits, for life (s 18BC, reg 4E)`
    `interim attendant care benefits (s 18BD, reg 4F), ending on` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `short-term attendant care benefits (s 18BB), for up to 1 year after the accident, ending on` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `no attendant care benefits: no impairment from the injury requiring attendant care (ss 18BB-18BD)`
    `no attendant care benefits: the services do not meet s 18BE`
    `no attendant care benefits: interim benefits were already had for this impairment (s 18BD(5)), and short-term benefits need no earlier assessment as eligible for them (s 18BB(1)(c))`
    `outside this encoding: the injury was suffered before 1 July 2014 (Subdivision 1, ss 18A, 18B)`

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN `Attendant care facts`
GIVETH AN `Attendant care answer`
`the attendant care eligibility for` `the facts` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `the day of the accident` `is before` `the 2014 amendments commenced`
        THEN `outside this encoding: the injury was suffered before 1 July 2014 (Subdivision 1, ss 18A, 18B)`
        IF NOT (`the facts`'s `suffers an impairment as a result of the injury` AND `the facts`'s `requires attendant care services in consequence of the impairment`)
        THEN `no attendant care benefits: no impairment from the injury requiring attendant care (ss 18BB-18BD)`
        IF NOT `the facts`'s `the services meet s 18BE`
        THEN `no attendant care benefits: the services do not meet s 18BE`
        IF `reg 4E is met`
        THEN `long-term attendant care benefits, for life (s 18BC, reg 4E)`
        IF `the facts`'s `has already had interim benefits for the same impairment`
        THEN `no attendant care benefits: interim benefits were already had for this impairment (s 18BD(5)), and short-term benefits need no earlier assessment as eligible for them (s 18BB(1)(c))`
        IF `reg 4F is met`
        THEN `interim attendant care benefits (s 18BD, reg 4F), ending on` `the interim end`
        OTHERWISE `short-term attendant care benefits (s 18BB), for up to 1 year after the accident, ending on` (`the day` 12 `months after` (`the facts`'s `the day of the accident`))
    WHERE
        `reg 4E is met` MEANS
                `the facts`'s `has an injury of a kind listed in Schedule 1`
            AND (    (`the facts`'s `meets the Schedule 1 criteria for that injury in full` AND `the facts`'s `the injury is permanent and stable`)
                 OR  `the facts`'s `the Commission considers exceptional circumstances warrant long-term benefits`)
        `reg 4F is met` MEANS
                `the facts`'s `has an injury of a kind listed in Schedule 1`
            AND (    (`the facts`'s `meets the Schedule 1 criteria for that injury, leaving aside any requirement of permanency` AND (NOT `the facts`'s `the injury is permanent and stable`))
                 OR  `the facts`'s `the Commission considers exceptional circumstances warrant interim benefits`)
        `the interim end` MEANS
            IF (`the age of a person born` (`the facts`'s `the date of birth`) `on` (`the facts`'s `the day of the accident`)) LESS THAN 3
            THEN `the day` 72 `months after` (`the facts`'s `the date of birth`)
            ELSE `the day` 36 `months after` (`the facts`'s `the day the claim was made`)

§§ `Part 5 -- payments in respect of death (ss 4, 20-24, 37; reg 4M)`

-- s 20: "qualifying person means: (a) a person who dies as a result of injuries received in a motor accident occurring in the
-- Territory; or (b) a resident of the Territory who dies as a result of injuries received in a motor accident, involving a Territory
-- motor vehicle, occurring outside the Territory." (b) has no "in Australia" (finding 4).
GIVEN `the place` IS AN `Accident place`
      `a resident of the Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a qualifying person, dying after an accident at` `the place` `being a resident` `a resident of the Territory` IF
        `the place`'s `occurred in the Territory`
    OR  (`a resident of the Territory` AND `the place`'s `arose out of the use of a Territory motor vehicle`)

-- s 4: "spouse, in relation to a person, means: (a) a spouse of the person who, at the relevant time, was living with the person on a
-- bona fide domestic basis; or (b) a spouse ... not living with the person on a bona fide domestic basis but, in the opinion of the
-- Commission, was wholly or substantially dependent upon the person at that time; or (c) a de facto partner ... for a continuous period
-- of at least 2 years immediately preceding that time; or (d) a de facto partner ... [of less than 2 years] but who, in the opinion of
-- the Commission, was wholly or substantially dependent upon the person at that time; or (e) if the person is an Aboriginal or Torres
-- Strait Islander: (i) a person referred to in paragraphs (a), (b), (c) or (d)); or (ii) an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander to
-- whom the person is married according to the customs and traditions of the particular community". READING: the relevant time is
-- the death.
DECLARE `Partner` HAS
    `was married to the person`                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `was the person's de facto partner`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `was living with the person on a bona fide domestic basis`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `had been the de facto partner for a continuous period of at least 2 years immediately before` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commission considers them wholly or substantially dependent on the person`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `both are Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islanders married by the customs of their community`   IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the partner` IS A `Partner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a spouse within s 4` `the partner` IF
        (`the partner`'s `was married to the person` AND `the partner`'s `was living with the person on a bona fide domestic basis`)
    OR  (`the partner`'s `was married to the person` AND `the partner`'s `the Commission considers them wholly or substantially dependent on the person`)
    OR  (`the partner`'s `was the person's de facto partner` AND `the partner`'s `had been the de facto partner for a continuous period of at least 2 years immediately before`)
    OR  (`the partner`'s `was the person's de facto partner` AND `the partner`'s `the Commission considers them wholly or substantially dependent on the person`)
    OR  `the partner`'s `both are Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islanders married by the customs of their community`

-- s 4: "child, of a person (the parent), includes: (a) an unborn child; or (b) a person in relation to whom the parent stands or stood
-- in loco parentis." "dependent child -- a child ... is a dependent child if: (a) the child: (i) has not attained the age of 16 years; or
-- (ii) has not attained the age of 21 years and is a full-time student or physically or mentally handicapped; and (b) the child is not
-- the spouse of another person; and (c) the child is dependent on the parent for financial support or, in the case of an unborn child,
-- there is a reasonable expectation that the child will be dependent".
DECLARE `Child` HAS
    `is the person's child, unborn child or a child to whom the person stood in loco parentis` IS A BOOLEAN
    `age in completed years`                                                                 IS A NUMBER
    `is a full-time student, or physically or mentally handicapped`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the spouse of another person`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `is dependent on the person for financial support, or for an unborn child is expected to be` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the child` IS A `Child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a dependent child within s 4` `the child` IF
        `the child`'s `is the person's child, unborn child or a child to whom the person stood in loco parentis`
    AND (    `the child`'s `age in completed years` LESS THAN 16
         OR  (`the child`'s `age in completed years` LESS THAN 21 AND `the child`'s `is a full-time student, or physically or mentally handicapped`))
    AND (NOT `the child`'s `is the spouse of another person`)
    AND `the child`'s `is dependent on the person for financial support, or for an unborn child is expected to be`

-- s 4: "dependent parent, in relation to a person, includes an adoptive parent, a stepfather, a stepmother, a grandfather, a
-- grandmother and a parent of the spouse of the person who, at the time of the accident, is primarily dependent on the person for
-- financial support."
GIVEN `a parent or one of the listed relatives` IS A BOOLEAN
      `was primarily dependent on the person for financial support at the accident` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a dependent parent within s 4, being` `a parent or one of the listed relatives` `and` `was primarily dependent on the person for financial support at the accident` IF
    `a parent or one of the listed relatives` AND `was primarily dependent on the person for financial support at the accident`

-- s 20A(1): "The Commission may reduce benefits payable under this Part if: (a) the accident resulting in the death of the qualifying
-- person occurred while that person was driving a motor vehicle; and (b) the qualifying person was under the influence of alcohol or
-- a drug to such an extent [as in s 9(1)(b)]; and (c) the influence of the alcohol or drug contributed, in the Commission's opinion,
-- to the accident." (2): the presumption, with reg 4M. (3): also if "(a) the accident occurred while the qualifying person was engaged
-- in conduct that created a substantial risk of injury to the qualifying person; and (b) the qualifying person recklessly ignored the
-- risk." (4): "a proportion of the benefits otherwise payable considered appropriate by the Commission". (5): "the Commission must reduce
-- the benefits in accordance with the regulations" -- but no regulation says how (finding 11): the proportion is the Commission's, an
-- INPUT. (6): "Benefits payable under section 22(1)(a) must not be reduced under this section."
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Part 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commission may reduce death benefits under s 20A for` `the facts` IF
        `s 9 applies` `the facts`
    OR  `s 9B applies` `the facts`

-- Death benefits are among "all benefits" that ss 9D-9G, 10 and 10A-10C exclude for an "injury or death"; ss 9-9C reach only loss of
-- earning capacity and impairment.
GIVEN `the exclusion` IS A `Part 3 exclusion`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `excludes death benefits` `the exclusion` IF
    CONSIDER `the exclusion`
    WHEN `no benefits are payable at all` `under` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `only medical and rehabilitation, long-term and interim attendant care and appliance benefits are payable` `under` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 22(1)(a): "to the person liable to meet the expense of the person's funeral -- the cost of the funeral or 5.2 times average weekly
-- earnings (whichever is the lesser amount)". Not reduced under s 20A (s 20A(6)). READING (finding 14): s 11(3)(c) names
-- "compensation under sections 22 and 23 for a death", which takes in the funeral benefit.
`the funeral multiple` MEANS 5.2

GIVEN `the cost of the funeral` IS A NUMBER
      `average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `s 11 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the s 11A entitlement set against it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 22(1)(a) funeral benefit for a funeral costing` `the cost of the funeral` `at average weekly earnings of` `average weekly earnings` `with s 11` `s 11 applies` `less` `the s 11A entitlement set against it` MEANS
    `after ss 11 and 11A,` (min `the cost of the funeral` (`the funeral multiple` TIMES `average weekly earnings`)) `with s 11` `s 11 applies` `less` `the s 11A entitlement set against it`

-- s 22(1)(b): "for the benefit of the qualifying person's spouse or dependent child (or spouse and dependent child) -- the prescribed
-- proportions of 156 times average weekly earnings at the time the payment is made." (4): "If, before dying as a result of the injury,
-- the qualifying person received compensation by way of lump sum for permanent impairment resulting from the same injury, the amount
-- of the benefit payable under subsection (1)(b) is to be reduced by the amount of that lump sum." READING (finding 12): (4) is part
-- of the amount otherwise payable; s 11, then s 20A (the Commission's proportion), then s 11A follow, and the result is shared.
`the death lump sum multiple` MEANS 156

DECLARE `Death lump sum facts` HAS
    `average weekly earnings when the payment is made`                         IS A NUMBER
    `there is a spouse`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of spouses (s 37)`                                             IS A NUMBER
    `the number of dependent children`                                         IS A NUMBER
    `the impairment lump sum the qualifying person received for the same injury` IS A NUMBER
    `s 11 applies`                                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the s 20A reduction the Commission determined`                            IS A NUMBER
    `the s 11A entitlement set against it`                                     IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Death lump sum answer` IS ONE OF
    `the s 22(1)(b) lump sum, in dollars` HAS `in total`                        IS A NUMBER
                                              `for each spouse`                 IS A NUMBER
                                              `for each dependent child`        IS A NUMBER
    `no s 22(1)(b) lump sum: there is no spouse and no dependent child`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Death lump sum facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 22(1)(b) total for` `the facts` MEANS
    max 0 (`after s 20A` MINUS `the facts`'s `the s 11A entitlement set against it`)
    WHERE
        `the amount otherwise payable` MEANS
            max 0 ((`the death lump sum multiple` TIMES (`the facts`'s `average weekly earnings when the payment is made`)) MINUS (`the facts`'s `the impairment lump sum the qualifying person received for the same injury`))
        `after s 11` MEANS `after ss 11 and 11A,` `the amount otherwise payable` `with s 11` (`the facts`'s `s 11 applies`) `less` 0
        `after s 20A` MEANS `after s 11` MINUS (`after s 11` TIMES (`the facts`'s `the s 20A reduction the Commission determined`))

-- s 22(3), the Table: "| Spouse | 100% |", "| one child | 100% |", "| 2 or more children | Equally between children |", "| Spouse
-- and one child | 10% to child, balance to spouse |", "| Spouse and not more than 5 children | 5% to each child, balance to spouse |",
-- "| Spouse and more than 5 children | 25% divided equally between children, balance to spouse |". READING (finding 7): a spouse and
-- one child are also "not more than 5 children"; the row that names one child governs. s 37(1), (2): for more than one customary
-- spouse, the benefit is what one marriage would give, "payable to such spouses in equal shares".
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Death lump sum facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the share of each dependent child, as a proportion, for` `the facts` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the children` AT MOST 0 THEN 0
        IF NOT `the facts`'s `there is a spouse` THEN 1 DIVIDED BY `the children`
        IF `the children` EQUALS 1 THEN 10%
        IF `the children` AT MOST 5 THEN 5%
        OTHERWISE 25% DIVIDED BY `the children`
    WHERE
        `the children` MEANS `the facts`'s `the number of dependent children`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Death lump sum facts`
GIVETH A `Death lump sum answer`
`the s 22(1)(b) lump sum for` `the facts` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the facts`'s `there is a spouse`) AND `the facts`'s `the number of dependent children` AT MOST 0
    THEN `no s 22(1)(b) lump sum: there is no spouse and no dependent child`
    ELSE `the s 22(1)(b) lump sum, in dollars` `the total` `each spouse's share` (`the total` TIMES `the child's share`)
    WHERE
        `the total` MEANS `the s 22(1)(b) total for` `the facts`
        `the child's share` MEANS `the share of each dependent child, as a proportion, for` `the facts`
        `the spouses' share` MEANS
            IF `the facts`'s `there is a spouse`
            THEN 1 MINUS (`the child's share` TIMES `the facts`'s `the number of dependent children`)
            ELSE 0
        `each spouse's share` MEANS
            IF `the facts`'s `there is a spouse`
            THEN (`the total` TIMES `the spouses' share`) DIVIDED BY (max 1 (`the facts`'s `the number of spouses (s 37)`))
            ELSE 0

-- s 23(1): "there shall be paid to or for the benefit of each dependent child of a deceased qualifying person an amount per week equal
-- to 10% of average weekly earnings at the time the payment is made." (2): "The aggregate of all amounts paid or payable per week under
-- subsection (1) shall not exceed average weekly earnings and where there are more than 10 dependent children ... they shall be
-- entitled in equal shares to an amount equal to average weekly earnings". s 11 reduces it; s 20A may. No end is stated (finding 15).
GIVEN `the number of dependent children` IS A NUMBER
      `average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `s 11 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the s 20A reduction the Commission determined` IS A NUMBER
      `the s 11A entitlement set against it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 23 weekly benefit for each of` `the number of dependent children` `children at average weekly earnings of` `average weekly earnings` `with s 11` `s 11 applies` `and s 20A` `the s 20A reduction the Commission determined` `less` `the s 11A entitlement set against it` MEANS
    IF `the number of dependent children` AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE max 0 (`after s 20A` MINUS `the s 11A entitlement set against it`)
    WHERE
        `the s 23 amount` MEANS
            IF `the number of dependent children` GREATER THAN 10
            THEN `average weekly earnings` DIVIDED BY `the number of dependent children`
            ELSE 10% TIMES `average weekly earnings`
        `after s 11` MEANS `after ss 11 and 11A,` `the s 23 amount` `with s 11` `s 11 applies` `less` 0
        `after s 20A` MEANS `after s 11` MINUS (`after s 11` TIMES `the s 20A reduction the Commission determined`)

-- s 24: "Where a qualifying person dies ... leaving the person surviving neither a spouse nor a dependent child but a dependent parent
-- or parents who normally resides or reside with the person, that parent or those parents shall be paid an amount equal to 156 times
-- average weekly earnings and, if more than one, in equal shares." s 11(3) does not name s 24 (finding 13); s 20A may reduce it.
GIVEN `there is a spouse or a dependent child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of dependent parents who normally resided with the person` IS A NUMBER
      `average weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the s 20A reduction the Commission determined` IS A NUMBER
      `the s 11A entitlement set against it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 24 benefit for each dependent parent, with a spouse or child surviving` `there is a spouse or a dependent child` `and` `the number of dependent parents who normally resided with the person` `parents, at average weekly earnings of` `average weekly earnings` `with s 20A` `the s 20A reduction the Commission determined` `less` `the s 11A entitlement set against it` MEANS
    IF `there is a spouse or a dependent child` OR `the number of dependent parents who normally resided with the person` AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE (max 0 (`after s 20A` MINUS `the s 11A entitlement set against it`)) DIVIDED BY `the number of dependent parents who normally resided with the person`
    WHERE
        `the s 24 amount` MEANS `the death lump sum multiple` TIMES `average weekly earnings`
        `after s 20A` MEANS `the s 24 amount` MINUS (`the s 24 amount` TIMES `the s 20A reduction the Commission determined`)

-- s 21: where a person who "would have been a qualifying person" had they died "is a full-time patient in a hospital or other
-- institution because of injuries received ... and, in the opinion of the Commission, the person is likely permanently to remain a
-- full-time patient ..., the Commission may, at the written request of the spouse of the person, determine that this Part shall apply",
-- and the person is "deemed to have died on the date of the determination".
GIVEN `would be a qualifying person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a full-time patient in a hospital or other institution because of the injuries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission considers the person likely permanently to remain a full-time patient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commission may apply Part 5 on the spouse's written request (s 21), where` `would be a qualifying person` `and` `is a full-time patient in a hospital or other institution because of the injuries` `and` `the Commission considers the person likely permanently to remain a full-time patient` IF
        `would be a qualifying person`
    AND `is a full-time patient in a hospital or other institution because of the injuries`
    AND `the Commission considers the person likely permanently to remain a full-time patient`

§§ `s 25 and regs 5, 6 -- commutation to a lump sum`

-- s 25: "If the regulations so provide, a liability to pay statutory benefits ... may be commuted, in accordance with the regulations,
-- to a liability to make a single payment by way of lump sum." Reg 5(1): "The Commission may commute a liability to pay compensation
-- for loss of earning capacity." (2): "(a) on the application of the eligible person; or (b) if the amount of the compensation ... does
-- not justify, in the Commission's opinion, the administrative cost of making periodic payments." (3): "a discount rate of 6% will be
-- applied" (the method is not given: finding 17). (4): payment "discharges the Commission from further liability". (5): "the
-- Commission has a discretion to re-open a commutation ... if: (a) the commutation was made without the eligible person's consent;
-- and (b) there has been a substantial deterioration of the eligible person's medical condition since the date of the commutation."
`the commutation discount rate` MEANS 6%

GIVEN `is entitled to compensation for loss of earning capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has applied for commutation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission considers the amount does not justify the cost of periodic payments` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commission may commute the weekly benefit under reg 5, for a person who` `is entitled to compensation for loss of earning capacity` `and` `has applied for commutation` `or where` `the Commission considers the amount does not justify the cost of periodic payments` IF
        `is entitled to compensation for loss of earning capacity`
    AND (`has applied for commutation` OR `the Commission considers the amount does not justify the cost of periodic payments`)

GIVEN `was made without consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition has substantially deteriorated since` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commission may re-open a reg 5 commutation made` `was made without consent` `where` `the condition has substantially deteriorated since` IF
    `was made without consent` AND `the condition has substantially deteriorated since`

-- Reg 6(1): it "applies to statutory benefits of the following kinds: (a) compensation for loss of earning capacity under section 13 of
-- the Act; (b) compensation for the reasonable cost of medical and rehabilitation services under section 18 of the Act; (c) long-term
-- benefits for attendant care services under section 18B of the Act." Section 18B is the long-term benefit for injuries before 1 July
-- 2014; s 18BC, for later injuries, is not named (finding 16). (2): "on application by an eligible person ... if satisfied that: (a)
-- the eligible person is ordinarily resident outside Australia or is about to leave Australia to take up residence, for a substantial
-- period, outside Australia; and (b) the eligible person is entitled to benefits of the kind for which commutation is sought; and (c)
-- ... the degree of the permanent impairment (as assessed by the Commission) is 15% or more; and (d) the eligible person's medical
-- condition has stabilised". (4): "The total amount ... cannot exceed $1million (indexed) and the component ... for the reasonable cost
-- of medical and rehabilitation services cannot exceed $300 000 (indexed)." Reg 3: "(indexed) indicates that the sum ... is to be
-- adjusted to reflect changes in the CPI between 1 July 2007 and 1 July in the financial year in which the relevant motor accident
-- occurred." The CPI figures are INPUTS.
DECLARE `Commutable benefit` IS ONE OF
    `compensation for loss of earning capacity (s 13)`
    `medical and rehabilitation compensation (s 18)`
    `long-term attendant care benefits`

DECLARE `Reg 6 facts` HAS
    `the day of the accident`                                                         IS A DATE
    `has applied`                                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `is ordinarily resident outside Australia, or about to leave to live outside it for a substantial period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the assessed percentage of permanent impairment of the whole person`             IS A NUMBER
    `the medical condition has stabilised so its future course can be predicted with reasonable certainty` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts`   IS A `Reg 6 facts`
      `the benefit` IS A `Commutable benefit`
      `is entitled to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commission may commute under reg 6, on` `the facts` `the benefit` `if entitled` `is entitled to it` IF
        `the kind is one reg 6 names`
    AND `the facts`'s `has applied`
    AND `the facts`'s `is ordinarily resident outside Australia, or about to leave to live outside it for a substantial period`
    AND `is entitled to it`
    AND `the facts`'s `the assessed percentage of permanent impairment of the whole person` AT LEAST 15
    AND `the facts`'s `the medical condition has stabilised so its future course can be predicted with reasonable certainty`
    WHERE
        `the kind is one reg 6 names` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the benefit`
            WHEN `long-term attendant care benefits` THEN `the facts`'s `the day of the accident` `is before` `the 2014 amendments commenced`
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- A reg 3 "(indexed)" sum: the sum scaled by the CPI for 1 July in the financial year of the accident over the CPI for 1 July 2007.
GIVEN `the sum` IS A NUMBER
      `CPI for 1 July 2007` IS A NUMBER
      `CPI for 1 July in the financial year of the accident` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reg 3 indexed amount of` `the sum` `from CPI` `CPI for 1 July 2007` `to CPI` `CPI for 1 July in the financial year of the accident` MEANS
    `the sum` TIMES (`CPI for 1 July in the financial year of the accident` DIVIDED BY `CPI for 1 July 2007`)

`the reg 6(4) total cap before indexation` MEANS 1000000
`the reg 6(4) medical cap before indexation` MEANS 300000

§§ `Claims and review -- the dates`

-- s 31(2): "The Commission may refuse to consider: (a) a claim in respect of an accident; or (b) a claim for the variation of a benefit,
-- made later than 6 months after the date of the accident or the occurrence giving rise to the claim for variation". (3): it "shall
-- refuse to consider" such a claim "made: (c) later than 3 years after the date of the accident or the occurrence ...; or (d) in the
-- case of a claimant who had not attained the age of majority at the time of the accident or the occurrence ..., later than 3 years
-- after the date the claimant attained the age of majority." READING (finding 18): the Act does not define the age of majority; it is
-- 18 under the Age of Majority Act 1974 (NT), which is not deposited.
`the age of majority` MEANS 18

GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE
      `the claimant's date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for a claim the Commission must not refuse, for an accident on` `the day of the accident` `and a claimant born` `the claimant's date of birth` MEANS
    IF (`the age of a person born` `the claimant's date of birth` `on` `the day of the accident`) LESS THAN `the age of majority`
    THEN `the day` 36 `months after` (`the day` (`the age of majority` TIMES 12) `months after` `the claimant's date of birth`)
    ELSE `the day` 36 `months after` `the day of the accident`

GIVEN `the day of the accident` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day before the Commission may refuse a claim, for an accident on` `the day of the accident` MEANS
    `the day` 6 `months after` `the day of the accident`

DECLARE `Claim timing answer` IS ONE OF
    `in time: made within 6 months, so the Commission may not refuse it for lateness (s 31(2))`
    `late: made more than 6 months after, so the Commission may refuse to consider it (s 31(2))`
    `too late: the Commission must refuse to consider it (s 31(3))`

GIVEN `the day the claim is made` IS A DATE
      `the day of the accident` IS A DATE
      `the claimant's date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Claim timing answer`
`the s 31 timing of a claim made on` `the day the claim is made` `for an accident on` `the day of the accident` `by a claimant born` `the claimant's date of birth` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the outer limit` `is before` `the day the claim is made`
        THEN `too late: the Commission must refuse to consider it (s 31(3))`
        IF `the six month mark` `is before` `the day the claim is made`
        THEN `late: made more than 6 months after, so the Commission may refuse to consider it (s 31(2))`
        OTHERWISE `in time: made within 6 months, so the Commission may not refuse it for lateness (s 31(2))`
    WHERE
        `the outer limit` MEANS `the last day for a claim the Commission must not refuse, for an accident on` `the day of the accident` `and a claimant born` `the claimant's date of birth`
        `the six month mark` MEANS `the last day before the Commission may refuse a claim, for an accident on` `the day of the accident`

-- s 31A: "The Commission may refuse to consider a claim in respect of an accident made by the driver of a motor vehicle if the driver
-- did not report the motor accident in accordance with regulation 19(2) of the Traffic Regulations 1999, unless, in the opinion of the
-- Commission, the driver had a reasonable excuse for not doing so." The Traffic Regulations are not deposited.
GIVEN `was the driver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reported the accident as reg 19(2) of the Traffic Regulations 1999 requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission considers there was a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commission may refuse the claim under s 31A of a claimant who` `was the driver` `and` `reported the accident as reg 19(2) of the Traffic Regulations 1999 requires` `with excuse` `the Commission considers there was a reasonable excuse` IF
        `was the driver`
    AND (NOT `reported the accident as reg 19(2) of the Traffic Regulations 1999 requires`)
    AND (NOT `the Commission considers there was a reasonable excuse`)

-- s 28A(2): "The claimant must request the review within 90 days after: (a) receipt of notice of the original decision; or (b) if
-- notice of the original decision is not given -- the claimant becomes aware of the decision."
`the days to ask for a review` MEANS 90

-- s 28B(1)(c): "make a decision on the request (a review decision) within 30 business days after the request is made or that period as
-- extended under subsection (3)". (3): if the designated person "requests a conference or additional information, the period ... is
-- extended by the lesser of the following: (a) the period equal to the period between the giving of the notice making the request and
-- the holding of the conference or giving of the information; (b) the period equal to the period between the giving of the notice and
-- the period stated in the notice". READING (finding 19): "business day" is not defined in the Act; the Interpretation Act 1978 (NT)
-- is not deposited. A business day is taken as a weekday that is not a Territory public holiday; the public holidays are counted by
-- the claimant (an INPUT), and the extension, in calendar days, is added after the 30th business day.
`the business days for a review decision` MEANS 30

GIVEN `the day the request is made` IS A DATE
      `weekday public holidays in the period` IS A NUMBER
      `a conference or information was requested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days from that notice to the conference or the information` IS A NUMBER
      `days from that notice to the time it stated` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the review decision on a request made` `the day the request is made` `with` `weekday public holidays in the period` `holidays, a conference or information requested` `a conference or information was requested` `taking` `days from that notice to the conference or the information` `of` `days from that notice to the time it stated` MEANS
    `the day` `the extension` `days after` (`the weekday` (`the business days for a review decision` PLUS `weekday public holidays in the period`) `weekdays after` `the day the request is made`)
    WHERE
        `the extension` MEANS
            IF `a conference or information was requested`
            THEN min `days from that notice to the conference or the information` `days from that notice to the time it stated`
            ELSE 0

-- s 28E(3): the notice referring the matter to the Tribunal "must be given within 28 days after: (a) [for a review decision] (i)
-- receipt of notice of the review decision ...; or (ii) if notice ... is not so given -- the claimant becomes aware of the decision; or
-- (b) [where no review decision is made in time] -- the end of the period provided under section 28B."
`the days to refer to the Tribunal` MEANS 28

§§ `Regulative rules -- the claimant, the Commission and the designated person`

-- Clock: days, counted from the day each rule starts. The Commission and the designated person are the scheme's statutory decision
-- makers and get no seat; their duties appear as what the claimant is owed and by when.
DECLARE `MACA party` IS ONE OF `the claimant`, `the Commission`, `the designated person`

DECLARE `MACA act` IS ONE OF
    `claim damages or compensation under the law of the place of the accident`
    `give the Commission written notice of the claim`
    `reimburse the Commission` HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER
    `make the claim in the approved form`
    `report the accident as reg 19(2) of the Traffic Regulations 1999 requires`
    `ask the designated person to review the original decision`
    `make the review decision`
    `refer the matter to the Tribunal`

-- s 7(3): a person entitled under s 7(2) "may elect to claim damages or compensation under the law of the jurisdiction in which the
-- accident occurred and, if such a claim is made: (a) the claimant must immediately give the Commission written notice of the claim;
-- and (b) the claimant's entitlement to statutory benefits ceases; and (c) if statutory benefits have already been paid ...: (i) the
-- Commission is, to the extent of the payment, subrogated to the rights of the claimant on the claim; and (ii) the claimant must
-- reimburse the Commission from damages or compensation (if any) awarded on the claim for the amount of the statutory benefits already
-- paid." Claiming is a choice (DO ... LEST FULFILLED). READING (finding 9): "immediately" is the same day. The repayment has no period.
GIVEN `statutory benefits already paid` IS A NUMBER
      `damages or compensation awarded` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `MACA party` `MACA act`
DECIDE `s 7(3) -- a claimant who claims in the other jurisdiction must tell the Commission at once, and repay benefits from what is awarded` IS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    DO    `claim damages or compensation under the law of the place of the accident`
    HENCE
        (PARTY  `the claimant`
         MUST   `give the Commission written notice of the claim`
         WITHIN 0
         LEST   BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 7(3)(a): the claimant must immediately give the Commission written notice of the claim")
        RAND
        `the repayment`
    LEST  FULFILLED
    WHERE
        `the amount to repay` MEANS `the s 7(3)(c)(ii) reimbursement of` `statutory benefits already paid` `from` `damages or compensation awarded`
        `the repayment` MEANS
            IF `the amount to repay` GREATER THAN 0
            THEN PARTY `the claimant`
                 MUST  `reimburse the Commission` (EXACTLY `the amount to repay`)
                 LEST  BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 7(3)(c)(ii): the claimant must reimburse the Commission, from the damages or compensation awarded, for the statutory benefits already paid"
            ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 31(1): a claim "shall be made as soon as practicable after the accident"; (1A): "in an approved form"; (3): the Commission "shall
-- refuse to consider" one made after the s 31(3) limit. Clock starts on the day of the accident (or of the occurrence for a variation);
-- the seat works out the days to the limit. The 6-month mark of s 31(2) is a function above: the Commission's permission to refuse.
GIVEN `days to the s 31(3) limit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `MACA party` `MACA act`
DECIDE `s 31 -- a claim must be made as soon as practicable, and the Commission must refuse one made after the s 31(3) limit` IS
    PARTY  `the claimant`
    MUST   `make the claim in the approved form`
    WITHIN `days to the s 31(3) limit`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 31(3): the Commission must refuse to consider a claim made later than 3 years after the accident, or for a claimant then under age, 3 years after reaching majority"

-- s 31A: the driver's report under reg 19(2) of the Traffic Regulations 1999. Those Regulations are not deposited, so the days they
-- allow are an INPUT. A claimant who was not the driver owes nothing here.
GIVEN `was the driver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days the Traffic Regulations allow for the report` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `MACA party` `MACA act`
DECIDE `s 31A -- a driver must report the accident as the Traffic Regulations require, or the Commission may refuse the claim` IS
    IF `was the driver`
    THEN PARTY  `the claimant`
         MUST   `report the accident as reg 19(2) of the Traffic Regulations 1999 requires`
         WITHIN `days the Traffic Regulations allow for the report`
         LEST   BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "s 31A: a driver who did not report the accident as reg 19(2) of the Traffic Regulations 1999 requires may have the claim refused, unless the Commission considers there was a reasonable excuse"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- ss 28A, 28B, 28E: a claimant "who is aggrieved by a decision ... may ask the designated person to review" it, within 90 days of
-- notice (s 28A(2)); the designated person "must ... make a decision on the request (a review decision) within 30 business days" as
-- extended (s 28B(1)(c), (3)); the claimant "may refer the matter to the Tribunal" within 28 days after notice of the review decision,
-- or after the end of the s 28B period if none is made (s 28E). Clock starts on receipt of notice of the original decision; asking and
-- referring are choices (DO ... LEST FULFILLED). READING: notice of the review decision is taken to be received on the day it is made.
-- L4 starts the rule under LEST when it first sees the deadline has passed (an event or a WAITUNTIL after it), and counts the 28 days
-- from then; the seat gives the exact last day.
GIVEN `days from the request to the review decision deadline` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `MACA party` `MACA act`
DECIDE `ss 28A, 28B, 28E -- ask for review within 90 days, a review decision within 30 business days, then the Tribunal within 28 days` IS
    PARTY  `the claimant`
    DO     `ask the designated person to review the original decision`
    WITHIN `the days to ask for a review`
    HENCE
        PARTY  `the designated person`
        MUST   `make the review decision`
        WITHIN `days from the request to the review decision deadline`
        HENCE
            PARTY  `the claimant`
            DO     `refer the matter to the Tribunal`
            WITHIN `the days to refer to the Tribunal`
            LEST   FULFILLED
        LEST
            PARTY  `the claimant`
            DO     `refer the matter to the Tribunal`
            WITHIN `the days to refer to the Tribunal`
            LEST   FULFILLED
    LEST   FULFILLED
